# WHAT VERCEL DOES NOT NEED A COPY OF, ON EVERY DEPLOYMENT.
#
# Vercel uploads the repository and keeps it with the deployment. Only the Vite
# build reads anything here, and it reads `src/`, `public/`, `api/` and the
# config files — nothing else in this list is opened during `npm run build`.
#
# EVERY PATTERN IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, AND THAT IS NOT STYLE.
#
# This file uses .gitignore matching rules, where a pattern with no leading
# slash matches a directory of that name AT ANY DEPTH. The first version of
# this file said `assets/`, meaning to exclude the 91 MB of art masters at the
# repo root — and it also matched `public/assets/`, which is everything the app
# serves. It shipped, and every image on the live site 404'd: card art, the
# field book plates, the tool-panel banners, the hero backdrop. The build
# succeeded and the deployment went Ready, because nothing here is imported by
# the bundle — Vite copies `public/` verbatim and never opens it, so an empty
# `public/` is not a build error.
#
# A leading slash anchors the pattern to the repository root, which is the only
# place any of these actually live. Keep it on every line.

# Art masters. Input to scripts/build-*.py, run by hand on a dev machine.
# NOT public/assets — see above.
/assets/

# The Python analytics service. Deployed to the VPS by scp, never by Vercel —
# see "THE PYTHON API DOES NOT SHIP WITH THE FRONTEND" in CLAUDE.md.
/server/

# Design records and runbooks.
/docs/
/MECHANISM.md
/DECK_TUNER.md

# Tests. `tsc -b` covers only src, vite.config.ts and api, so this is safe.
/tests/
/supabase/

# Local build tooling.
/scripts/

/video/
/dist/
